## Project Overview ##
	Thought stream is going to be a digital diary. 
    Part one is mostly just focusing on the back end API calls and developments. 
    We are creating read create update and delete operations for managing the diary entries. 
    Including some searching and filtering capabilities and weather data integration with open Weather API.

## Setup Instructions ##
    Update Your .env File With Propper Vars
    Run The Following:
```bash
    cd diary-app
    npm install
```
    Then Run One Of These
```bash
    npm start
    npm run dev
```

## Files ##
    ReadMe.txt - This File!
    db.js - MongoDB Connection Setup
    diaryController.js - Handles Read, Create, Update, And Delete Logic For Diary Entries
    weatherController.js - Fetches Weather Data From OpenWeather API
    DiaryEntry.js - Schema For Diary Entries
    diaryRoutes.js - Defines API Endpoints
    .env.example - Environment variables 
    .gitignore - Specifies Files To Ignore
    package.json - Project Metadata And Dependencies
    server.js - Main Entry Point For The Express Server
    Screenshots/.. - All Example API Calls

## Environment Variables ##
	MONGO_URI= Your MongoDB connection string (local or Atlas)
    PORT= Port Number (default 5000)
    OPENWEATHER_API_KEY= Your_openweather_api_key    

## Common Issues & Debugging Tips ##
	A Issues I Keeped Encountering Was Port Issues So I Added A Print 
    You Should See When Starting To Run:
    ```
    Server running on port "Port"
    MongoDB Connected: "Num"
    ```

## API Usage Guide ##
    Base URL: "http://localhost:<Port#>"
    GET : Can Be Searched By Location, Tag, Or Keyword
    
## Endpoints ##
Method : Endpoint         : Description                       ;
-------:------------------:-----------------------------------;
GET    : /api/diary       : Fetch All Diary Entries           ;
GET    : /api/diary/:id   : Fetch A Single Diary Entry By ID  ;
POST   : /api/diary       : Create A New Diary Entry          ;
PUT    : /api/diary/:id   : Update An Existing Diary Entry    ;
DELETE : /api/diary/:id   : Delete A Diary Entry              ;

